        It's my first project in the round larger than a water bottle bag, and the increases are really obvious,but I'm too lazy to frog it.
        Now that I realize increasing in the same spot
        <em>does</em> make an obvious difference, I will be staggering them in my next project.
      </p>
      <picture>
        <source media="(width < 1024px)" srcset="../images/pill-bottle-crochet-200.jpg">
        <source media="(width < 1500px)" srcset="../images/pill-bottle-crochet-1k.jpg">
        <img src="../images/pill-bottle-crochet-1k.jpg.jpeg" alt="Photo of orange ball of yarn positioned above a roughly circular orange crochet fabric with paperclips marking its rows along one of its radii.">
      </picture>
    </section>
  </main>
  <footer></footer>
</body>
</html>
{% endblock %}